$grp PS_MissionDescription : "{3136BE42592F3B1B}PrefabsEditable/MissionDescription/EditableMissionDescription.et" {
 SUM {
  coords 3086.754 86.25 6742.292
  m_sTitle "Summary"
  m_sTextData "The annual Track Mania race has come to Ruha. Who'll take home the cup and claim victory this year?"\
  ""\
  "- A casual and easy going mission ideal for seeding or end of play session missions. Not recommended for prime play."\
  ""\
  "<h2>NOTES</h2>"\
  "• Minimum of two drivers required."\
  "• Try to keep racing teams equal so it's balanced."\
  "• CIVFOR is completely optional. Primarily to be spectators, but also each role can serve a minimal purpose in the mission."
  m_bEmptyFactionVisibility 1
 }
 MN {
  coords 3086.754 86.25 6742.292
  m_sTitle "Mission notes"
  m_sTextData "<h2>END CONDITIONS</h2>"\
  "You can win by either:"\
  "Being the first team to complete 16 laps."\
  "or"\
  "Having the last remaining driver on your team."\
  ""\
  "<h2>NOTES</h2>"\
  "<b>• It is forbidden to kill unslotted roles to take the gear</b>"\
  "<b>• ALL CIVS APART FROM THE ACTING REFEREE ARE NOT ALLOWED TO USE THE RACE CONTROL CONSOLE TO REMOVE PLAYERS. IT IS STRICTLY FORBIDDEN AND DIRECTLY AGAINST MISSION INTENT</b>"\
  ""\
  "- A casual and easy going mission ideal for seeding or end of play session missions. Not recommended for prime play."\
  "Made by TheLocalPub. Leave suggestions, issues, and compaints in the #feedback channel on Discord."\
  ""
  m_bEmptyFactionVisibility 1
  m_bShowForAnyFaction 1
  m_iOrder 10
 }
 RacerBrief {
  coords 3086.754 86.25 6742.292
  m_sTitle "Track Brief"
  m_sTextData "<h2>HOW TO PLAY</h2>"\
  "We have 1min to drive our car to the starting line. (Rear wheel drive)"\
  "Each team must complete 16 laps of the track. The first team to complete all 16 laps will be declared the winner."\
  "There are only winners and losers in this world. There is no second or third place. You're either first or nothing."\
  ""\
  "<h2>RULES</h2>"\
  "<b>Failure to follow these rules may result in your team being eliminated from the tournament at the discretion of the referee</b>"\
  "<b>Three strikes and you're out!</b>"\
  ""\
  "<h3>Drivers:</h3>"\
  "• Vehicles must not intentionally collide with other vehicles or personnel. Minor touches that are obviously not deliberate can pass."\
  "• Only <b>ONE</b> vehicle per team may be on the track and considered in play at any one time."\
  "- A broken-down vehicle remaining on the track is still considered in play. The pit crew must be deployed to repair the vehicle, or the team's secondary vehicle may be deployed once the primary vehicle has gone <b>OFF THE TRACK.</b>"\
  "• Drivers cannot use the pit to race through. If a car enters the pit, it must come to a full stop at least once before leaving."\
  ""\
  "<h3>Pit Crews:</h3>"\
  "• Pit crews must remain in the pit at all times unless their driver's vehicle has broken down and requires repair, or the driver requires recovery for any reason."\
  ""\
  "<b>If all teams agree, \"Derby\" mode can be enacted where all rules are dropped in favour of a free for all.</b>"
  m_bShowForAnyFaction 1
  m_iOrder 2
 }
 SIT {
  coords 3086.754 86.25 6742.292
  m_sTitle "Situation"
  m_sTextData "<h2>PRELIMS</h2>"\
  "DTL: 22/07/1971, 1500hrs, Horse Track, Ruha."\
  "Weather: Clear and dry. Local forecasting has suffered from recent funding cuts, so expect unpredictable and potentially unannounced weather changes."\
  ""\
  "<h2>LORE</h2>"\
  "The annual Track Mania International Speedway Championship has arrived in Ruha, bringing the world's finest drivers together for another year of high-speed competition."\
  "Three finalists remain: the Blue Boosters, Red Racers, and Green Gasers. Engines are warmed, pit crews are standing by, and the track is ready."\
  "Sixteen laps stand between the teams and the trophy. There are no points, no podium positions, and no consolation prizes."\
  "Who will cross the finish line first and claim the Track Mania International Championship?"
  m_bShowForAnyFaction 1
  m_iOrder 1
 }
 GameMechs {
  coords 3086.754 86.25 6742.292
  angles 0 1 0
  m_sTitle "Gameplay mechanics"
  m_sTextData "<h2>REFEREE'S CONSOLE</h2>"\
  "A console only the <b>ACTING REFEREE</b> has permission to use on the top floor of the red viewing building. It has the ability to:"\
  "• Disqualify each team at his disgression. This deletes their cars and deletes unslotted roles. Alive players will remain."\
  "• Ability to spawn explosive barrels on the track after 6mins will be activated. These will appear as transparent barrels with no collision for 10 seconds before spawning the real thing."\
  "• Spawn fireworks."\
  ""\
  "<h2>PIT CREW & REPAIRS</h2>"\
  "• Vehicles can be fully repaired within 15m of their pit building."\
  "• One Jerry can and a spare wrench are on the workbench in the pits"\
  "- Each crew member spawns with 1 wrench."\
  "• A repair truck can be used to go recover their teams vehicle on the track. This should be loaded with repair \"supplies\" by interacting with the rear while close to the pit."\
  "• A fuel tank next to the pit can be used to refill jerry cans (Drop it on the floor next to it and look at the can)"\
  ""\
  "<h2>BANANAS</h2>"\
  "The currency of Ruha are Bananas. These don't have proper function as of yet, but use these to barter/trade with light roleplay."
  m_bShowForAnyFaction 1
  m_iOrder 4
 }
 CivRoleSum2 {
  coords 3086.754 86.25 6742.292
  angles 0 1 0
  m_sTitle "Civilian roles summary"
  m_sTextData "<h2>SPECTATORS</h2>"\
  "Take your seat in the stands, get a better view track-side, chat with your friends, or grab some team merch from the vendor to show your support. If you're feeling particularly mischievous, you might even find a way to help your team through more <i>nefarious</i> means."\
  ""\
  "• Be a good sport, lean into the light roleplay, craft a silly little story, and most importantly, have fun."\
  ""\
  "<h2>REFEREE</h2>"\
  "The Ref calls the shots. He's an expert in the <i>Track Brief</i> and won't miss a thing. <b>Three strikes and you're out!</b>"\
  ""\
  "• The Referee's control console, located at the top of the red viewing stand/building, allows him to disqualify teams from the race, and also play with pyrotechnics like fireworks."\
  "After 6mins the acting Ref can spice up the race by spawning explosive barrels."\
  "<b>EVERYONE EXCEPT THE ACTING REFEREE ARE FORBIDDEN FROM USING THE CONSOLE TO REMOVE PLAYERS. THIS IS STRICTLY AGAINST MISSION INTENT.</b>"\
  ""\
  "<h2>SECURITY</h2>"\
  "Security are responsible for maintaining order, ensuring the teams can race uninterrupted, and keeping the crowd safe from troublemakers. All orders should be given clearly and directly."\
  ""\
  "<b>• Lethal force is authorised against anyone endangering drivers, pit crews, or attendees through direct or indirect actions, including negligence or possession of weapons.</b>"\
  "<b>- This includes obstructing vehicles in motion which could cause a crash.</b>"\
  "• Security may cuff and detain anyone refusing an order for up to <b>5 minutes.</b>"\
  "• Security may use physical force against anyone causing serious disruption or repeatedly refusing orders."\
  ""\
  "<h2>VENDOR</h2>"\
  "The vendor is here to buy and sell team merchandise and other items for a price. Bananas are the currency in Ruha, so keep your eyes open — there might be a few lying around."\
  ""\
  "• The vendor has permission to <i>fuck your shit up</i> if you steal his stock or attempt to scam him."\
  ""\
  "<h2>DOCTOR</h2>"\
  "The doctor has been employed by the racetrack to provide medical assistance throughout the event. Equipped with a medkit and his trusty ambulance, he's ready to help anyone who needs it. Respond to crashes, rescue dogs trapped in hot cars, and save the world!"
  m_bShowForAnyFaction 1
  m_iOrder 3
 }
}